SYSTEM_PATCH_V1
0. Patch intent

This patch updates the old documentation set so AI agents do not rebuild the old itinerary mistake.

Core correction

Old docs implicitly model:

Tour -> Destinations -> Service Items

New rebuild must model:

Tenant -> Tours -> TourStops -> Service Items
                    \-> Destinations (catalog/reference, optional)
Why

The old structure was good enough to compose one tour, but too rigid for repeated / scalable tour creation. The new rebuild must separate:

Destination = reusable location/catalog entity
TourStop = actual itinerary segment inside a tour
1. Canonical architecture change
1.1 Keep

Keep these modules as valid and reusable:

multi-tenancy
memberships
suppliers
service-item threads/messages
tasks/reminders
publish gate
billing gate
site studio
growth/SEO
mobile ops surface
1.2 Replace

Replace the old assumption:

destination is a tour-owned itinerary block

with:

destination is reusable catalog/reference
tour_stop is the itinerary block
2. Required model changes
2.1 New canonical entity: tour_stops

Add a new canonical entity:

TourStop
- id
- tenant_id
