Meaning

Examples:

Day 1: Hanoi Arrival
Day 2-3: Hanoi City Tour

These are not plain destinations.
They are itinerary blocks.

2.2 Redefine destinations

Old meaning:

destination row belongs directly to one tour
carries nights/arrival/departure

New meaning:

reusable catalog/reference location
can optionally power content defaults / labels / suggestions
not the primary itinerary unit anymore
New destination role
Destination
- id
- tenant_id
- code
- name
- is_active
- created_at
Notes
destination_texts stays valid
it now localizes catalog/reference content, not the stop itself
2.3 Service items must move from destination_id to tour_stop_id

Old docs and schema tie service items to destination.

This must change.

New rule

All operational service items belong to tour stop, not destination catalog.

Rename linkage:
destination_id -> tour_stop_id

For:

accommodations
meals
guides
local transports
intercity legs
Why

“Hanoi Arrival” and “Hanoi City Tour” may refer to the same Hanoi destination but require different services.

